<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|<tuple|notes|notes-meta>>

<\body>
  <notes-header>

  <chapter*|Papers>

  <notes-abstract|Preprints deposited here as an alternative to the usual
  archives (experimental).>

  This folder collects preprints of mine and of my co-authors. Each paper has
  a folder with its TeXmacs sources, an HTML version and a PDF. A metadata
  file records the SHA-256 hash of every source, the deposit date, the
  authors and the copyright notice, and points to the metadata of the
  previous version; this index records the SHA-256 hash of the current
  metadata file of each paper. See <hlink|the description of the
  metadata|metadata.tm>. The list below is generated from
  <hlink|index.json|index.json>, which records for each paper its current
  metadata file and the hash of that file; it is the entry point for programs.
  The arrangement is experimental and may change; it is
  the first archive in <hlink|OpenSheaf|https://opensheaf.org>, an open
  format for document archives and collections.

  All rights to the papers are reserved to their authors.

  <paper-index>

</body>

<\initial>
  <\collection>
    <associate|page-medium|paper>
  </collection>
</initial>
